        ['Dashboard', '/dashboard', ['can_view_dashboard_menu'],
            'Overview of sales, receipts, stock and alerts for the company.'],
        ['Customers (CRM)', '/customers', ['can_view_customers_menu'],
            'Customer list. Add one with "Add Customer" (business name, contacts, KRA PIN, region/county/town, payment method; credit customers fill the credit application). A customer is always shown by their business / company name; the contact person only appears where labelled Contact. Click a customer to open their profile: Orders, Invoices, Account (balance, open invoices, unapplied payments, pending cheques), Statement and Notes. The Statement\'s ageing lists each unpaid invoice on its own line (S/No, invoice, invoice date, due date, days past due) with its balance under <30, 30-60, 60-90 or >90 days, counted from the due date: the days it has passed its payment date, and an invoice not yet due counts as 0 so it sits under <30. An invoice moves along as it gets more overdue and drops off once paid; with no unpaid invoices the statement has no ageing section at all. It is worked out as at the To date, after credit notes and receipts (oldest invoice first). Moving an order or invoice to another customer takes its credit notes and any receipt or cheque that paid only that invoice with it; a receipt that also paid other invoices stays with the old customer and goes on their oldest open invoices or their credit, so the moved invoice owes that part. Accountants can delete credit notes. Customers > Accounts lists credit accounts and limits; the GM, admins and accountants approve or reject an account or a credit limit change from the row\'s "..." menu. To delete a customer: the row\'s "..." menu > Delete Customer, then confirm (GM, admins and accountants; any customer). Everything recorded for that customer is deleted with them - orders, invoices, credit notes, receipts, cheques, quotes and collection notes (the box lists how many of each first); stock on their orders goes back, except past orders. It cannot be undone, so it is for clearing test or wrongly entered data. A customer statement is on the profile\'s Statement button; choose the period, then Download (Excel/PDF/CSV) or Print.'],
        ['Quotes', '/sales/quotes', ['can_view_quotes_menu'],
            'Sales > Quotes. "New Quote": pick the customer - or "One-time customer" in the customer list for someone not in the system: type just their name, the payment period (cash, 7-90 days, printed as the payment terms) and pick the Sales Rep (sales team); the quote shows them as "One-time customer". "Convert to Order" on such a quote asks which customer in the system the order goes under (the quote is merged into that customer); register them under Customers first if they are new. Then "Add Product" under the lines (the same search as on orders: type a description, item no. or code like NSPD 001 - matching price codes first, then one line per item at its NSPV price; a full code adds the line at once). Each line\'s code box can be retyped to change the item or use another list\'s code; set the quantity (price can be negotiated per quote), then save. Open a quote to view/print its document; "Convert to Order" turns an accepted quote into an order.'],
        ['Orders', '/sales/orders', ['can_view_sales_menu'],
            'Sales > Orders. "New Order": choose customer, order date, payment type (cash/credit), add products and quantities (prices come from the customer\'s price list), save. A credit order is always allowed: if the customer has credit invoices past their credit days, the form shows them in amber ("Overdue: ...") as a reminder to follow up the payment, but the order still goes ahead. An order is approved into an invoice (numbered NSK/####). Approvers: the GM, a Director, the Warehouse Manager or an Accountant - an accountant never approves an order they raised (Accountant A raises, Accountant B approves), and whoever raised it is not sent the approval alert. From an order you can create the dispatch. Past orders (dated on or before 31/10/2026) do not move stock.'],
        ['Invoices', '/sales/invoices', ['can_view_sales_menu'],
            'Sales > Invoices. Invoices are made from approved orders and numbered NSK/#### (from 02/11/2026 the series starts at NSK/0432). Open one to see lines, payments and balance; "View Document" shows the printable invoice with its delivery note, the invoice\'s Dated date and, above it, Invoice Date, the day it was entered in the system (kept compact: totals and VAT are the last rows of the items table, the Scan me QR sits beside the payment details, and it shows no amount paid or balance - those are on the invoice screen and the customer statement; when printed, an invoice that would spill onto a second page is shrunk to fit one page if it stays readable, down to 80%, about 10 lines, and a longer invoice keeps its normal size but is shrunk slightly when that removes a nearly empty last page); row menu > Download gives Excel/PDF/CSV. Tabs: "Delivery Invoices" (the transporters DI-##### invoices, paid with their Pay button or from Supplier Payments) and "Supplier Invoices" - what suppliers billed us (bills such as PUR-131, and their debit notes from the filter): date, supplier, total, paid, balance, status (unpaid / part paid / paid) and "Paid By", the supplier payments that paid each (e.g. PV-161). Search finds an invoice by number, supplier, description or the payment that paid it; click a row to see each payment and the amount it put on that invoice. Supplier invoices are made three ways: (1) goods received create one automatically (amount = quantity x buying price plus shipping/logistics and the PO VAT, supplier invoice no. = the receipt reference, due date from the supplier payment terms; it follows the receipt if the receipt is edited); (2) "Record Supplier Invoice" for bills that are not goods (services, rent): supplier, their invoice no., date, due date, amount, VAT, description and optional account code (blank = Inventory); (3) Template then Import (preview first) for many at once, including debit notes (Type = Debit Note). New ones are numbered on from PUR- (debit notes DN-) and can be paid from Supplier Payments. Export gives Excel (same columns as the import, so it can be edited and imported back), PDF or CSV. An unpaid recorded invoice can be deleted from its details; one from goods received changes with its receipt. Every tab pages 20 / 50 / 250 / All rows (Rows per page under the table) and exports Excel/PDF/CSV.'],
        ['Credit Notes', '/sales/credit-notes', ['can_view_sales_menu'],
