        ['Cheques', '/sales/cheques', ['can_view_sales_menu'],
            'Sales > Cheques: post-dated cheques received, their maturity, clearing or bouncing (a bounced cheque re-opens the invoices and adds a KES 2,000 charge). Tabs: "Cheques" and "Bounced Cheque Debit", which lists every bounced customer cheque with its debit from the earliest to date: S/No, Debit No. (DEB-001, DEB-002...; click it to open the document), date, customer, cheque no., bank, cheque amount, debit, paid, balance and status, with search, paging and Export (Excel/PDF/CSV). A debit has its own DEB series and takes no invoice number or NSK number, so it is not on the Filing page. It is not listed in Sales > Invoices, only on this tab. Otherwise it behaves as an invoice: it shows under its DEB number on the customer\'s Account and on their statement and ledger, and receipts pay it in date order with the invoices. A cheque is always accepted, however old the invoices it pays: the customer\'s PD cheque credit period is a recorded term and refuses nothing. It always pays the oldest invoice first, through to the newest.'],
        ['Receipts (customer payments)', '/payments', ['can_view_payments_menu'],
